speechtext:
Export Development Corporation states that: 1. The refinancing agreement signed on November 1, 1972 between the President of Pakistan and the Export Development Corporation for some $6.5 million was undertaken to provide Canada's share of debt relief established under a multilateral agreement among Pakistan's major creditors; the refinancing undertaken by EDC consolidates maturities falling due in the period from May 1971 to June 1973 under five separate financing agreements signed previously between EDC and Pakistan;
2.	With regard to the term, the last repayment of the amount refinanced will be due July 1, 1977;
3.	Interest, including accrued interest, is to be paid semi-annually from January 1, 1973; interest rates on Export Development Corporation long-term financing are not published since the disclosure of a rate established in respect of one transaction may seriously jeopardize current negotiations for export business; and
4.	Repayment of the amount consolidated is in six semiannual instalments beginning January 1,1975.
